  "report_period": "Week 41 (2nd Oct to 9th Oct 2026)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "The Capesize \"Ekaterini V\" 173/2012 Bohai, China (SS/DD 01/2027) was committed to Far Eastern interests at USD 35 mill. For reference, the \"Aanya\" 179/2012 HHIC, Philippines (SS/DD 06/2027) was sold a couple of months ago at USD 36,9 mill. BW Group have committed their Kamsarmax \"World Diana\" 82/2020 Oshima, Japan (SS 04/2030, DD 05/2028, Scrubber fitted) at USD 41 mill, while a week ago, the one-year-older \"Babitonga\" 81/2019 Tsuneishi, Japan (SS 10/2029, DD 10/2027) was committed at USD 38,5 mill basis delivery Feb'27. Furthermore, the \"Moon\" 80/2012 Stx, Korea (SS/DD 02/2027) was committed at USD 19,8 mill. Note that a month ago, the one-year-younger \"Daebo Gladstone\" 81/2013 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 12/2028) was sold at USD 22,5 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Oak\" & \"Juniper\" 57/2011 Stx Dalian, China (SS 03/2031, DD 02/2029 & SS 02/2031, DD 02/2029) were committed at USD 16,5 mill each. Remind you that back in August, the two-years-older sister vessel \"Lila Mundra\" 57/2009 Stx Dalian, China (SS 05/2029, DD 07/2027) was sold at USD 12,5 mill. Alphard Maritime have committed their Handysize \"AM Prestige\" 32/2014 Guangzhou, China (SS 01/2029, DD 03/2027) to undisclosed interests at USD 12,5 mill. For reference, the one-year-older \"Bianca\" 33/2013 Samjin, China (SS/DD 04/2028) was sold a month ago at mid USD 13 mill.",
    "tankers": "Nordic American Tankers committed their Suezmax \"Nordic Freedom\" 159/2005 Daewoo, Korea (SS 03/2030, DD 04/2028) at USD 65 mill, while the \"Ocean Start\" 158/2005 Hyundai Samho, Korea (SS/DD 06/2028, Scrubber fitted, Ice Class 1B) was committed a month ago at USD 47,4 mill. In addition, Dynacom Tankers have committed their \"Tianlong\" 159/2009 Bohai, China (SS 01/2029, DD 11/2026) at high USD 80's mill. By way of comparison, the \"Karolos\" 150/2009 New Times, China (SS 12/2029, DD 12/2027, Scrubber fitted) was committed a week ago at USD 92 mill. The MR2 \"Green Planet\" 50/2014 Dae Sun, Korea (SS 04/2029, DD 04/2027) was committed to undisclosed interests at USD 36,5 mill. Note that a month ago, the sister vessel \"LVM Aaron\" 51/2014 Dae Sun, Korea (SS 05/2029, DD 05/2027) was committed at USD 35,5 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "Iron ore rates on the West Australia to China route settled between USD 13.95/14.70 fio across Port Hedland, Dampier and Port Stanley departures. In the Atlantic, long-haul business from Tubarao to Qingdao, including West Africa options, fixed between USD 34.20/35.40 fio. Transatlantic runs from PDM, Port Cartier and Narvik to European destinations achieved between USD 13.50/19.50 fio, while a TRMT departure to Qingdao made USD 10.40 fio.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "In the Pacific, NoPac trips with Singapore-Japan and South East Asia options settled between USD 17,500/26,500 pd. An Australian round from South East Asia to Japan fetched USD 21,500 pd alongside a USD 300,000 ballast bonus. From West Coast India, trips via ECSA to South East Asia range fixed between USD 21,000/25,750 pd, while Indian Ocean runs via South Africa and Nacala obtained between USD 16,750/19,000 pd. Out of ECSA, front- haul fixtures to Singapore-Japan achieved between USD 22,650/24,500 pd with ballast bonuses from USD 1,265,000 to USD 1,400,000, whereas transatlantic grain runs to Continent and Mediterranean range reached between USD 33,650/38,500 pd. In the Atlantic, a Continent trip via USEC to Far East made USD 33,500 pd, alongside a scrap run to East Med securing USD 37,000 pd.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "In the Pacific, Indonesian coal trips to SE Asia and WCI ranges settled between USD 22,250/26,000 pd and USD 31,000 pd respectively. Nickel ore and clinker runs from South China to Far East and West Africa achieved between USD 18,500/26,500 pd, while an Australian nickel ore trip to China made USD 23,750 pd. Out of WCCA, a NoPac run to SE Asia fetched USD 23,000 pd with a USD 700,000 ballast bonus. Regional iron ore and limestone runs from ECI, WCI and PG ranges fixed between USD 12,000/20,000 pd, while South Africa coal to ECI reached USD 23,000 pd with a USD 230,000 ballast bonus. In the Atlantic, US Gulf coal to India reached USD 38,000 pd, with transatlantic grains fixing between USD 20,500/28,500 pd. A Continent scrap run to East Med achieved USD 37,000 pd and a Baltic trip to ECSA made USD 25,500 pd. ECSA front-haul grain and sugar trips to ECI and SE Asia ranged between USD 19,750/21,000 pd with ballast bonuses up to USD 1,100,000, alongside transatlantic grain to Med reaching USD 36,500 pd. On period, fixtures for 4 to 12 months duration settled between USD 21,000/23,500 pd.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "In the Pacific, regional runs from North China to South East Asia range fixed between USD 15,500/17,000 pd, while steel and project cargo departures from South China to WCCA and Continent range obtained between USD 21,500/22,000 pd. An East Australia trip to Japan achieved USD 19,000 pd and a WCCA grain run via Vancouver to Japan fetched USD 24,000 pd. In the Atlantic, USEC wood pellet runs to Continent range settled between USD 21,000/24,000 pd, an ECSA trip to Continent made USD 25,000 pd and a West Med departure to ECI reached USD 18,500 pd. On period, a Handymax delivering in ECSA fixed for 4 to 6 months duration at USD 20,000 pd."
    }
  },
